    s__COFFEE_BITTER(py_str("Bitter coffee is over-extracted: grind it coarser, let the water come off the boil for half a minute, and take it off the grounds sooner - about 4 minutes in a cafetiere, 25 to 30 seconds for an espresso. Sour is the same dial the other way and wants a finer grind, hotter water and a little longer. Stale beans and a dirty machine make both, and instant tastes bitter when it is made with boiling water - let the kettle rest first."));
    s__COFFEE_SOUR(py_str("Sour coffee is under-extracted: grind it finer, use water just off the boil rather than boiling, and give it longer on the grounds - about 4 minutes in a cafetiere, 25 to 30 seconds for an espresso. Bitter is the same dial the other way and wants a coarser grind and a shorter brew. A sour note that only shows up with milk is usually the milk."));
